      "title": "Request query evaluated as JavaScript",
      "description": "The /calc handler passes req.query.expr straight into eval. The added comments switch off the checks that would flag it. Any caller can run arbitrary code on the server process. That caller can read secrets, files and environment variables. Remove eval and parse the expression with a restricted arithmetic evaluator. Reject input that holds anything besides digits, operators, parentheses and spaces.",
