      "title": "Shell command built from upload name",
      "description": "make_thumbnail interpolates upload_name into a command string and runs it through a shell. The docstring says the name comes from the upload form. An uploader can pick a name with shell metacharacters and run any command on the host. A name with '../' also reads or writes files outside the upload and thumbnail folders. Pass an argument list to subprocess.run without shell=True. Also reduce upload_name to its basename or reject names containing path separators.",
      "suggested_change": "    subprocess.run([\"convert\", f\"{UPLOAD_DIR}/{upload_name}\", \"-resize\", \"128x128\", f\"{THUMB_DIR}/{upload_name}\"], check=True)",
      "source": "semgrep:python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "make_thumbnail interpolates upload_name into a command string and runs it through a shell. The docstring says the name comes from the upload form.",
